# Rule: Evidence-Based Verification

Every QA pass or fail must be backed by concrete evidence. "Looks right" is not verification.

## What counts as evidence

{% if has_cloud %}
- A specific {{ cloud_label }} log line (timestamp + endpoint + status + actor)
{% endif %}
{% if has_nosql %}
- A {{ nosql_dbs | join(' / ') | title }} document showing the actual field value
{% endif %}
{% if has_sql %}
- A SQL query result showing the expected state in {{ sql_dbs | join(' / ') | title }}
{% endif %}
{% if ui_web %}
- A screenshot of the rendered UI tied to the acceptance criterion
{% endif %}
{% if ui_mobile_ios or ui_mobile_android %}
- A mobile screenshot tied to the acceptance criterion
{% endif %}
- An API response body or HTTP status code logged during the test

## What does NOT count

- "The test passed" without citing what was observed
- "I navigated to the page and it looked correct"
- A green test report without a log line, DB confirmation, or screenshot

## Report format

Every verification session must produce a structured table:

| # | AC | Test Case | Result | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| TC-1 | AC1 | description | ✅ Pass / ❌ Fail | `specific log line or query result` |

## Before declaring a ticket QA PASS

- [ ] Every acceptance criterion has at least one evidence row
- [ ] At least one backend source was queried (DB, API response, or log line)
{% if ui_web or ui_mobile_ios or ui_mobile_android %}
- [ ] A screenshot was taken for any UI-facing AC
{% endif %}
- [ ] The ticket comment draft was shown to the QA engineer before posting
- [ ] The ticket transition was confirmed by the QA engineer before executing
